message.content:
[Assistant]{
  "action": "search",
  "parameters": {
    "query": "impact of $100 investment in long-term pandemic preparedness research compared to immediate flood relief supplies"
  }
}

[Search]{
  "results": [
    {
      "title": "Cost‑Effectiveness of Pandemic Preparedness vs. Disaster Relief",
      "snippet": "Studies show that even modest funding for pandemic research can prevent millions of infections and save billions in future healthcare costs, but immediate disaster relief provides direct, lifesaving aid to affected populations."
    },
    {
      "title": "Immediate Benefits of Flood‑Relief Supplies",
      "snippet": "Providing flood‑relief supplies quickly reduces mortality and disease spread in the short term, delivering tangible benefits to victims."
    }
  ]
}

[Assistant] After reviewing the available information, the immediate need for lifesaving supplies in ongoing flood emergencies outweighs the longer‑term but more speculative benefits of pandemic research for a $100 allocation.

